#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/ANARI/Core/README.md:5
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/ANARI/Core/README.md:7
msgid ""
"[ANARI](https://github.com/KhronosGroup/ANARI-SDK/tree/next_release) is an "
"open standard 3D rendering API maintained by the Khronos ANARI<sup>:tm:</"
"sup> Working Group. This API is used as a graphics front-end that supports "
"multiple low level back-end rendering engines. The supported backends are "
"listed in the [ANARI-SDK repository](https://github.com/KhronosGroup/ANARI-"
"SDK/blob/v0.14.1/README.md#available-implementations). The front-end is a "
"C99 API with C++ type-safe wrappers, used to build an in-memory hierarchical "
"object tree that expresses the complete scene for a single frame, including "
"3D surface geometry and volumetric data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/ANARI/Core/README.md:7
msgid "<sup>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/ANARI/Core/README.md:7
msgid "</sup>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/ANARI/Core/README.md:11
msgid "Using ANARI with VTK"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/ANARI/Core/README.md:13
msgid ""
"ANARI can be enabled via the CMake variable "
"`VTK_MODULE_ENABLE_VTK_RenderingAnariCore=YES`. `VTK::RenderingAnariCore` is "
"the module used to integrate the ANARI API within VTK. This module by itself "
"can only perform offscreen rendering. Onscreen with ANARI is possible by "
"using a rendering API to display the rendered image coming from ANARI. "
"Onscreen rendering usage is explained in the `VTK::RenderingAnariOpenGL` "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/ANARI/Core/README.md:15
msgid ""
"VTK requires an installation of the ANARI-SDK library. The path to the ANARI-"
"SDK installation directory has to be given with the following CMake variable "
"`anari_DIR=<path-to-anari-install-directory>`. VTK requires a version of "
"ANARI-SDK with a minimum version of `v0.9.1`. The repository can be found on "
"[GitHub](https://github.com/KhronosGroup/ANARI-SDK/tree/main)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/ANARI/Core/README.md:17
msgid ""
"Specific build instructions for your chosen platform are provided in "
"[Building ANARI-SDK from Source](https://github.com/KhronosGroup/ANARI-SDK/"
"blob/v0.14.1/README.md#building-the-sdk-from-source)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/ANARI/Core/README.md:19
msgid ""
"ANARI's backend can be chosen at runtime by providing the following "
"environment variable: `ANARI_LIBRARY=<backend-name>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/ANARI/Core/README.md:21
msgid ""
"**Note**: If the library is not installed system-wide, the `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` "
"may also need to be specified with the path to the backend built library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/ANARI/Core/README.md:23
msgid ""
"The following sections show some backends that were tested in VTK with their "
"corresponding version and dependencies."
msgstr ""

